<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sack of Antwerp (1576)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1576">1576</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Spanish Fury at Antwerp</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a>, known as the Spanish Fury, took place on 4 November 1576, when mutinous, long-unpaid Spanish troops of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-flanders">Army of Flanders</a> stormed and plundered the city for three days. Several thousand inhabitants were killed and much of the city was burned. The outrage drove the provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> to unite against Philip II in the Pacification of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghent">Ghent</a> four days later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sack-of-antwerp-1576.jpg" alt="Sack of Antwerp (1576)" width="320" height="265" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:De_Spaanse_Furie,_anoniem,_ca_1585,_MAS.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
